  "body": "Red in the full suite at 1b579ca4f on mote (`go test -tags nogui -timeout 45m ./...`, run alone on the machine after the other suites there ended; every other package ok):\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestCancelledSignInEndsItsFetch (0.30s)\n    plugin_signinend_test.go:134: the fetch failed with \"\", want AbortError\nFAIL\tgithub.com/yetone/magpie/internal/plugin\t351.099s\n```\n\nThe test added with 441a2b6b1 (#5016). `markedWithin(home, \"fetch-aborted\", …)` passed, so the file existed, but `os.ReadFile` read it empty: likely the marker is created before its contents are written (seen by the poll between open and write), so the check can read a half-written file. Waiting for the content (or writing the marker through temp + rename) would fix the class. Not reproduced alone; unrelated to the router change in that commit.",
  "closed_by": null,
